{
  "id": "boyle_s_law__mariotte_s_law_",
  "title": "Boyle's Law (Mariotte's Law)",
  "description": "Calculate the volume and pressure relationships of ideal gases at constant temperature using Boyle's Law (Mariotte's Law), where P₁V₁ = P₂V₂",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Boyle's Law (Mariotte's Law)\n\nBoyle's law states that for a perfect gas at constant mass and temperature, the volume varies inversely with absolute pressure:\n\n**P₁V₁ = P₂V₂**\n\nWhere:\n- **P** = absolute pressure (Pa, psi, MPa, etc.)\n- **V** = volume (m³, ft³, etc.)\n- **Subscript 1** = initial state\n- **Subscript 2** = final state"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "P1",
          "label": "Initial Pressure (P₁)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 2,
          "unit": "MPa"
        },
        {
          "id": "V1",
          "label": "Initial Volume (V₁)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 1,
          "unit": "m³"
        },
        {
          "id": "P2",
          "label": "Final Pressure (P₂)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 4,
          "unit": "MPa"
        },
        {
          "id": "V2",
          "label": "Final Volume (V₂)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 0.5,
          "unit": "m³"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "constant",
          "label": "PV Constant",
          "formula": "inputs.P1 * inputs.V1",
          "unit": "MPa·m³",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "calc_P2",
          "label": "Calculated Final Pressure (P₂)",
          "formula": "(inputs.P1 * inputs.V1) / inputs.V2",
          "unit": "MPa",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "calc_V2",
          "label": "Calculated Final Volume (V₂)",
          "formula": "(inputs.P1 * inputs.V1) / inputs.P2",
          "unit": "m³",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}